{"content":"Root cause: `IndexedSet.__eq__` in boltons/setutils.py had an inverted comparison (`set(self) != set(other)` instead of `==`) in its fallback branch for non-IndexedSet comparisons. This caused `difference_update`'s `if self in others: self.clear()` guard to misfire whenever `self in others` was evaluated via `__eq__` against a different set-like object, wiping the set and producing `[]` instead of the correct remaining elements — matching both reported failures ('bulk difference update' and 'small difference update unchanged').

Fix applied: changed `return set(self) != set(other)` to `return set(self) == set(other)` in `__eq__` (boltons/setutils.py).

